{"type":"standard","title":"Tammari language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Tammari language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q35186","titles":{"canonical":"Tammari_language","normalized":"Tammari language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Tammari language</span></span>"},"pageid":33214276,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/B%C3%A9nin-Promotion_de_la_litt%C3%A9rature_en_ditammari.jpg/330px-B%C3%A9nin-Promotion_de_la_litt%C3%A9rature_en_ditammari.jpg","width":330,"height":220},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/B%C3%A9nin-Promotion_de_la_litt%C3%A9rature_en_ditammari.jpg/3840px-B%C3%A9nin-Promotion_de_la_litt%C3%A9rature_en_ditammari.jpg","width":5472,"height":3648},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1263005219","tid":"6aeb9489-b9ce-11ef-a271-602a449b24ab","timestamp":"2024-12-14T03:49:28Z","description":"Gur language of Benin and Togo","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tammari_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tammari_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tammari_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Tammari_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tammari_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Tammari_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tammari_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Tammari_language"}},"extract":"Tammari is a language which is spoken in Benin and Togo. It is also known as Ditammari. The Tammari people, who live in Benin and Togo, mostly speak the language. There are about 47,000 speakers. About half live in Togo, the other half in Benin. Ditammari is one of the Gur languages.","extract_html":"<p><b>Tammari</b> is a language which is spoken in Benin and Togo. It is also known as <b>Ditammari</b>. The Tammari people, who live in Benin and Togo, mostly speak the language. There are about 47,000 speakers. About half live in Togo, the other half in Benin. Ditammari is one of the Gur languages.</p>"}